# Home Page and Theme Conventions

The home page is a `mode: custom` MDX layout built with Tailwind classes.
Mintlify loads every root-level `.css` and `.js` file automatically, so
`style.css`, `academy.css`, and `search.js` need no registration.

## Structure

```text
index.mdx      # mode: custom; search + Ask AI entry, three tab cards, "Get started" list
style.css      # app shell colors, topbar pills, sidebar tweaks (theme.css overrides)
academy.css    # Academy card outline and sidebar duration tag
search.js      # wires data-search-trigger / data-assistant-trigger to Mintlify's own buttons
sidebar.js     # empty Settings sidebar title; Mintlify drops a group with no pages
```

## Patterns

- `index.mdx` uses Tailwind utilities with `dark:` variants for every color.
  Icons come from the built-in `<Icon icon="..." />` (Lucide).
- The custom search and Ask AI buttons carry `data-search-trigger` and
  `data-assistant-trigger`; `search.js` forwards clicks to Mintlify's
  `#search-bar-entry` and `#assistant-entry` (and their `-mobile` variants).
- The "Get started" list links to the first Guides pages in reading
  order. Update it when the Introduction or first feature group changes.
- CSS overrides target Mintlify's stable ids and classes
  (`#content-container`, `.nav-logo`, `#search-bar-entry`) and use
  `!important` only where the theme already sets the property. Keep a comment
  above each block naming what it overrides and why.
- Light and dark values sit next to each other: `.selector {}` then
  `.dark .selector {}`.

## Boundaries

- No content in `index.mdx` beyond entry points; articles live in the tabs.
- No feature-specific CSS in `style.css`; Academy styling stays in
  `academy.css`, and a new feature file gets its own `<name>.css`.
- No DOM changes in `search.js` other than click forwarding. Do not replace
  Mintlify's search or assistant.
- Do not add a third root JS file without a comment explaining what it hooks.
